In this document we have presented measurements of the inclusive and differential fiducial cross sections for the Higgs boson production
in the $H \rightarrow 4\ell$ decay channel in proton collisions at center-of-mass energies of 7~TeV and 8~TeV.
The measurements are performed using \usedLumiA of proton 7~TeV collision data and \usedLumiB of proton 8~TeV collision data.
%, recorded with the CMS detector at LHC.
The differential measurements have been performed as a function of the transverse momentum and the rapidity of the four-lepton system, transverse momentum of the leading jet, distance in rapidity between the Higgs boson candidate and the leading jet,
the invariant masses of the two lepton pairs, the five helicity angles formed by the leptons in the Collins-Soper frame,
and the  jet multiplicity.
Measurements of the inclusive cross section of Z boson production in the $Z \rightarrow 4\ell$ decay channel, as well as its ratio to the $\Hllll$ fiducial cross section, have also been performed using the 8~TeV collision data.
The results have been corrected for the detection efficiency and resolution effects to allow for direct comparison with the theoretical predictions.
The uncertainty on the unfolded result due to the underlying model assumption on the Higgs boson production and its properties has been estimated by studying a range of exotic Higgs boson production and spin-parity models, and it has been found that it is up to 7\% for the total fiducial cross section.
The fiducial cross section for the Higgs boson production in the $H \rightarrow 4\ell$ decay channel is measured to be $0.56^{\rm +0.67}_{\rm -0.44} \, {\rm(stat.)}\, ^{\rm +0.21}_{\rm -0.06}\,  {\rm (sys.)}$ and $1.11^{\rm +0.41}_{\rm -0.35} \, {\rm(stat.)}\, ^{\rm +0.14}_{\rm -0.10}\,  {\rm (sys.)}$ fb at 7~TeV and 8~TeV, respectively.
Results of all measurements have been compared with the SM-based theoretical calculations and no significant deviation has been observed.
